# Maven reads .mvn/*.config verbatim; a CRLF checkout would append a carriage return to the
# last token on each line, turning -D...=true into the string "true\r", which Boolean.getBoolean
# reads as false. Pin LF so the flags mean the same thing on the Windows CI legs.
.mvn/maven.config text eol=lf
.mvn/jvm.config text eol=lf

# The report script carries a shebang, and a CRLF checkout would make the interpreter line end
# in a carriage return. It is only ever invoked as `python3 <path>` today, which survives that,
# but pinning it costs nothing and removes the trap.
.github/scripts/*.py text eol=lf
